<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dessau</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dessau-Roßlau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dessau is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mulde">Mulde</a> joins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>. It was the residence of the princes of Anhalt-Dessau from 1603 and the capital of the united Duchy of Anhalt from 1863. In the 20th century it was home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/junkers">Junkers</a> aircraft works and, from 1925 to 1932, to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bauhaus">Bauhaus</a> school of design, whose building by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walter-gropius">Walter Gropius</a> is a World Heritage Site. It was merged with Roßlau in 2007.</p></div>
